    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Necropolis Knights.</strong> This warrior of Tomb Kings of Khemri enters the field with a complete D&D 5e profile: armor, hit points, weapons, racial traits, and tactical maneuvers are all resolved directly from the embedded items on this actor. Its battlefield presence is practical rather than ornamental: auras name their radius, diseases name their saving throws, and maneuvers state their action economy.</p><p>Use the inventory as the creature’s tactical menu. Weapons list finished attack or saving throw text; features describe the exact condition, movement, advantage, damage, recharge, or aura they create.</p><blockquote><p>“Dust remembers kings better than flesh ever could.”<br><em>— Settra</em></p></blockquote><p><strong>Wargear and battlefield powers.</strong> This creature enters battle with Battlefield Doctrine, Khopesh, Ancient Spear, Warbow, Chariot Blade, Greatbow, Hooves and Wheels, Lance, Necromantic Undead, Deathless Will, Whirlwind Sweep, Positional Trip. Its drilled responses, charms, blades, and battlefield rites shape the rhythm of its turns.</p>",
